      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing the Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed by selecting Google Cloud Monitoring as the external provider. This should provide a good base for the project. Next steps will involve solidifying how I identify the provider in the Python file, and begin to focus on implementing the time-window query. I will also make sure the user can easily switch to a different provider in the future.\n\n\n**Defining the Query File**\n\nI'm now focusing on creating `query_metric_window.py` and have included the necessary imports, along with a skeleton for the main function. Specifically, I'm integrating the Google Cloud Monitoring API. The provider's identity will be through the `google.cloud.monitoring_v3` import and `MetricServiceClient`. This should set the stage for later query implementation.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863928231,
          "start": 1789863924969
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc3414e9001RHtEudJZT5kR66",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc340fd9001ZwDMTZrS0iYk0M",
      "session_id": "ses_f43cbf0a4ffelgGA2G4jbAciAB",
      "time_created": 1789863924969,
      "time_updated": 1789863928231
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "556nyEwExPMj3sOV",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import monitoring_v3\nfrom google.protobuf import timestamp_pb2\nimport datetime\n\ndef query_metric_window(project_id: str, metric_type: str, minutes_ago: int = 5):\n    \"\"\"\n    Queries recent datapoints for a named metric over a time window using Google Cloud Monitoring.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: The Google Cloud project ID.\n        metric_type: The full metric type (e.g., \"compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/utilization\").\n        minutes_ago: The number of minutes from now to query data for. Defaults to 5 minutes.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = monitoring_v3.MetricServiceClient()\n    project_name = f\"projects/{project_id}\"\n\n    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    end_time = timestamp_pb2.Timestamp()\n    end_time.FromDatetime(now)\n\n    start_time = timestamp_pb2.Timestamp()\n    start_time.FromDatetime(now - datetime.timedelta(minutes=minutes_ago))\n\n    interval = monitoring_v3.TimeInterval(\n        end_time=end_time,\n        start_time=start_time,\n    )\n\n    query = f\"metric.type=\\\"{metric_type}\\\"\"\n\n    results = client.list_time_series(\n        name=project_name,\n        filter=query,\n        interval=interval,\n        view=monitoring_v3.ListTimeSeriesRequest.TimeSeriesView.FULL,\n    )\n\n    time_series_data = []\n    for ts in results:\n        for point in ts.points:\n            time_series_data.append({\n                \"metric\": ts.metric.type,\n                \"value\": point.value.double_value if point.value.HasField(\"double_value\") else point.value.int64_value,\n                \"timestamp\": point.interval.end_time.isoformat(),\n                \"resource_labels\": {k: v for k, v in ts.resource.labels.items()},\n                \"metric_labels\": {k: v for k, v in ts.metric.labels.items()},\n            })\n    return time_series_data\n",
            "filePath": "query_metric_window.py"
          },
